---
slug: mcp-admin/token-revoke
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  Operator revokes a bearer token by id (spec §20). Sets status:revoked — the next
  request carrying that token fails authentication. Operator-gated; the same control
  the token owner has on /mcp-tools, but exposed to operators for ANY token (the
  console's kill-switch for a misbehaving agent). Idempotent: revoking an already
  revoked token is a no-op. The token digest is never exposed here — only its id.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function is_admin = 'modules/mcp/commands/is_operator'
  unless is_admin
    response_status 403
    echo 'Forbidden'
    return
  endunless

  assign tid = context.params.id
  if tid != blank
    graphql _ = 'modules/mcp/tokens/revoke', id: tid
  endif

  redirect_to '/mcp-admin?tab=tokens'
-%}
